<section class="inchy-guide__row"><h2>01 / QUALITY<br>BEGINS AT THE SOURCE.</h2><div>
<p>Before there is a powder, there is a plant—and someone who tends it. INCHY begins with sacha inchi grown by farmers in Colombia.</p>
<p>Premium, high-quality sacha inchi was difficult to source. That’s why we helped establish a growers association. Working directly with its members gives our process a shared starting point: care for the seed and a commitment to quality.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="inchy-guide__row"><h2>02 / THE SEED,<br>GIVEN A NEW FORM.</h2><div>
<p>Our proprietary process has been developed over years of working with sacha inchi. Pressing removes part of the seed’s oil. Grinding and drying transform the remaining material into a powder, bringing its protein and fiber into a form that can be used in everyday preparations.</p>
<p>The transformation is deliberate. We work with the seed’s character, paying attention to how it tastes, how it feels and how it mixes. Our aim is a simple ingredient, carefully made.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="inchy-guide__row"><h2>03 / THE DETAILS<br>YOU EXPERIENCE.</h2><div>
<h3>FLAVOR.</h3><p>Sacha inchi has a taste of its own. We develop FORM1 with that character in mind. Unflavored means the seed’s own flavor remains part of the experience.</p>
<h3 class="inchy-spaced-heading">TEXTURE.</h3><p>Grinding changes the size of the seed particles. That matters to the feel of a powder in a spoonful of yogurt, a bowl of oats or a blended drink. Texture is part of our development, alongside composition.</p>
<h3 class="inchy-spaced-heading">PREPARATION.</h3><p>A functional ingredient must fit into something you actually enjoy. FORM1 is designed to mix into everyday foods and drinks. Different preparations give different results; in a thin drink, some settling can occur. Stir again or blend thoroughly.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="inchy-guide__row"><h2>04 / KEEP WHAT<br>BELONGS TOGETHER.</h2><div>
<p>Protein and fiber begin together in the seed. We keep both in the finished ingredient. This relationship guides the way we develop INCHY FORM1.</p>
<p>Processing changes the seed’s structure. Our purpose is to carry its protein and fiber into a useful new form, with respect for where they began.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="inchy-guide__row"><h2>05 / WHAT MAKES<br>IT INCHY?</h2><div>
<p>FORM1 is defined by the work behind it: direct sourcing, our proprietary process and development centered on taste, texture and everyday preparation.</p>
<p>Sacha inchi flours vary in how they are made. The word “flour” alone tells you little about that work. With INCHY, the purpose is specific: a functional nutraceutical ingredient that keeps protein and fiber together and fits into your routine.</p>
<p>One remarkable seed. A considered transformation. INCHY FORM1.</p>
